{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Issues in the Workplace", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "What Do You Think?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 15, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Describe  necessity, duty, advice, or strong disapproval in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to print out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to use a computer printer to print something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I printed out extra copies in case more people showed up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about responsibilities at work.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to sit through", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bstay until the end of an \u200bevent such as a \u200bmeeting or presentation ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: To be honest, I wasn't expecting a lot of people to show up let alone sit through the presentation. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to ramble on ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200btalk in a \u200bconfused way, often for a \u200blong \u200btime", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I may have been rambling on for all I know. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to overanalyze", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to examine something in \u200bdetail more than it needs to be in \u200border to \u200bdiscover more about it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you will overanalyze this, you won't get anywhere.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to come across", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bbehave in a way that makes \u200bpeople \u200bbelieve that you have a \u200bparticular \u200bcharacteristic", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You might have came across a bit too strong. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to set out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bstart an \u200bactivity with a \u200bparticular \u200baim", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:I won't have accomplished what I set out to do!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "If-Clauses Expressing Strong Disapproval", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you talk about conditions, you use if-clauses. You can use these to express different opinions or emotions about what someone else <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">did/does/will do</span></span> or<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> says/said/will say</span></span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You sometimes use <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">will</span></span> and <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">won't</span></span> in the if-clause to express strong disapproval. When someone insists on doing something, and you disagree with it, you can express that feeling.  </br></br>For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">If you<span class=\"strong\"> will </span>drive carelessly, you must be expecting to have an accident. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you won't calm down, you must accept that I'm not telling you what I thought.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you will correct them, you not only interrupt their train of thought but it will also affect their confidence.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you will keep up with this, you must have a chat with Denise.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you will overanalyze this, you won't get anywhere.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you will hand out a survey, you must be prepared for both positive and negative feedback.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you won't put time and effort into this, you must expect to see no changes around the office. ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Modals in the Past to Speculate the Possibility of Something", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to talk about the possibility of something happening or not, you can use modals.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The modals for speculating about past possibility are:</br></br>may (not) have </br> might (not) have</br> could (not) have</br> will (not) have", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:  </br></br><span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">may have </span>already done it, for all we know. </br>The boss <span class=\"strong\">won't have</span> had the chance to look over the report yet. </br>That wasn't a good idea - you <span class=\"strong\">might have</span> caused more trouble! </br> You <span class=\"strong\">could have </span>done just enough to finish.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Notice you use the past participle after each of these modal phrases.  </br></br> Look at the examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I may have been rambling on for all I know. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You might have come across a bit too strong. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I could have included a few more here and there now that I think about it. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I won't have accomplished what I set out to do!", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I discuss issues related to work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write slides for a presentation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my presentation to a small group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I answer questions about my topic.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "You need to make a presentation to a group of people at work. With a partner, discuss which topics would be appropriate.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose one topic.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Prepare a PowerPoint presentation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Prepare 5 slides with key words (not full sentences).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Insert images into your presentation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your presentation to a small group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Answer questions from the audience.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn10le15ob05re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn10le15ob05re2img01.jpg", "time": "1", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Mr. Green, could you hear me alright? Did you get a copy of my handout? I printed out extra copies in case more people showed up. To be honest, I wasn't expecting a lot of people to show up, let alone sit through the presentation. Was it okay? I may have been rambling on for all I know.<br><span class=\"strong\">Leonard</span>: If you won't calm down, you must accept that I'm not telling you what I think.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: You're right. Okay ... I'm calm.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Leonard</span>: You seem a bit frazzled."}, {"image": "engenn10le15ob05re2img05.jpg", "time": "25000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I'm just worried my presentation wasn't received well because everyone looked so bored. They may have been more interested in my presentation if there were some more visuals. I could have included a few more here and there now that I think about it.<br><span class=\"strong\">Leonard</span>: If you will overanalyze this, you won't get anywhere. Seeing that everyone around me was alert and listening, I wouldn't say they were bored.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: As I stood at the front of the room, I could see everyone's reactions. Most people didn't seem interested at all.<br><span class=\"strong\">Leonard</span>: You could have just been worried and overthinking it which is what I think. However, you might have come across a bit too strong.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: What do you mean? Was this when people were asking questions?<br><span class=\"strong\">Leonard</span>: Yes. If you will correct them constantly, you may not only interrupt their train of thought but it also affects their confidence."}, {"image": "engenn10le15ob05re2img06.jpg", "time": "72600", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I guess ... I'll never know what they were thinking. Unless ... I hand out a survey!<br><span class=\"strong\">Leonard</span>: If you will hand out a survey, you must be prepared for both positive and negative feedback.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I ought to just ask people what they thought in person.<br><span class=\"strong\">Leonard</span>: Hmm ... if you will keep up with that, you must have a chat with Denise.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I should just give up then!<br><span class=\"strong\">Leonard</span>: Don't do that. If you won't put time and effort into this, you must expect no one else will.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: That's true and I won't have accomplished what I set out to do!"}], "audiosrc": "engenn10le15ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le15ob05re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about solving problems in the workplace.", "type": "L